## SECTION 9: PRODUCT POSITIONING

### What Makes LineageLens Unique

No other tool tracks the provenance of AI-generated code. Tools exist that review code for bugs, security issues, or style. None answer:

**"This function was written by an AI — which one, in response to what prompt, with what model, and what risk signals did the generated code contain at insertion time?"**

LineageLens is the first system that captures provenance at insertion time, stores it persistently, and surfaces it at review time — including inside the AI conversation itself via the MCP server.

### Differentiation from Traditional Debugging Tools

| Traditional Debugging | LineageLens |
|---|---|
| Looks at what code does | Looks at where code came from |
| Operates at runtime or static analysis | Operates at write time |
| Knows the author is a human | Knows which AI tool wrote it |
| Requires a bug to exist | Captures context before a bug appears |
| No concept of "prompt" | Stores the prompt that produced the code |
| No model provenance | Tracks model name, version, parameters, session |
| Requires context switching | MCP tools surface provenance in-chat |

### Key Value Propositions

**For developers:** When something goes wrong in AI-generated code, know exactly what was asked, what the model produced, and what the surrounding context was — without reconstructing it from memory. Ask the MCP tools from inside any AI conversation to look up provenance without switching tabs.

**For engineering leads:** See your team's AI coding patterns: which models, which files, how much, what risk level — across all developers in the workspace. The timeline and graph views make AI insertion patterns visible at a glance.

**For compliance/security teams:** AI-generated code is in your codebase. LineageLens gives you the audit trail to prove what was generated, when, by which model, and whether it contained sensitive patterns at insertion time. Export as CSV for evidence packages.

