## APPENDIX: WHAT EVERY FILE DOES

### VS Code Extension (`lineagelens-src/`)

**`lineagelens-src/extension.ts`**
Main activation point for the VS Code extension. Registers all commands, starts the file watcher, initializes the local LLM proxy, creates the storage service (local or backend), and wires together the sidebar webview, hook listener, and provenance builder. On VS Code startup, this is the first file that runs.

**`lineagelens-src/proxy.ts`**
Local HTTP/HTTPS proxy running on port 8080 inside the extension process. Intercepts outbound LLM API traffic from any tool running on the machine. Captures request and response bodies for supported providers (Anthropic, OpenAI, GitHub Copilot, Codeium, OpenRouter, Sourcegraph, Google, AWS). Passes captures to the correlation engine. Separate from the universal proxy — this one is embedded in the extension.

**`lineagelens-src/correlation.ts`**
Correlation engine. Given a file insertion event (from the file watcher), it searches recent proxy captures for a matching LLM request/response pair within a 30-second window (`correlation.windowMs` default: 30000 ms). Uses timing proximity, file context, and Levenshtein text similarity to score candidate pairs. Also checks the Claude Code hook event buffer. Returns a `PromptCorrelationResult` with a confidence score and capture status (`full`, `metadata_only`, `tunnel_only`, `unavailable`).

**`lineagelens-src/eventSchema.ts`**
TypeScript type definitions for the provider-agnostic provenance event schema (`lineagelens.provenance-event.v1`). Defines `ProviderAgnosticProvenanceEvent`, `NormalizedAgentContext`, `PromptCorrelationResult`, and all supporting types. All adapters and capture paths produce records conforming to this schema. Versioned for future migration support.

**`lineagelens-src/lightweightRecord.ts`**
Pure TypeScript helper with no VS Code dependency. Accepts a minimal payload and returns a fully-formed `ProviderAgnosticProvenanceEvent`. Designed for use from CLI scripts, CI jobs, or other editor integrations that don't have access to the full extension context. Automatically infers `promptStatus`, synthesizes `PromptCorrelationResult`, and sets `shimName: 'lightweight-adapter'`.

**`lineagelens-src/hookListener.ts`**
Watches `~/.lineagelens/hook-events.jsonl` for Claude Code tool-use events written by a hook capture script. Reads new events on a polling interval and buffers them for the correlation engine. Enables full prompt capture for Claude Code sessions even when the proxy produces a `tunnel_only` record (because Claude Code hooks fire independently of the TLS layer).

**`lineagelens-src/contextSnapshot.ts`**
Captures a snapshot of the current workspace context at the moment of an AI insertion. Reads the active document, open files, environment variables (filtering secrets by name pattern), import statements, git branch, and AST structure using Tree-sitter. The snapshot is stored in the provenance record to provide context for future explanation and review.

**`lineagelens-src/backend.ts`**
HTTP client for the LineageLens backend. Sends provenance records via WebSocket (`/ws/capture`) with HTTP POST (`/ingest`) fallback. Manages the WebSocket connection lifecycle, retry logic, and connection health. Also handles backend authentication (token storage, refresh) and provides typed API client methods for search, explain, insights, and team endpoints.

**`lineagelens-src/backendAuth.ts`**
Authentication layer for the VS Code extension's backend connection. Stores JWT access and refresh tokens in VS Code Secret Storage (OS keychain). Handles token refresh before expiry. Parses JWT expiry from the `exp` claim to schedule proactive refresh. Exposed as a singleton so all backend calls share the same auth state.

**`lineagelens-src/agentAdapters/registry.ts`**
Adapter registry. Holds the ordered list of all 10 adapters. Given a `ProvenanceEvent`, runs all adapters in parallel and selects the result with the highest confidence score. Ties broken by adapter order (lower order = higher priority). Returns a `NormalizedAgentContext` or a fallback unknown context.

**`lineagelens-src/agentAdapters/shared.ts`**
Shared utilities for all adapters. Includes `inferProvider` (resolves AI provider from host + model name), `clampConfidence` (bounds confidence to [0, 1]), path-matching regex utilities, and the `NormalizedAgentContext` builder helpers used by every adapter.

**`lineagelens-src/agentAdapters/cursor.ts`**
Cursor IDE adapter. Detects Cursor by `x-cursor-*` request headers, `cursor` user-agent substring, and `composer` payload markers. Extracts Cursor-specific session IDs and conversation IDs. Reports `sessionKind: 'agentic'`.

**`lineagelens-src/agentAdapters/copilot.ts`**
GitHub Copilot adapter. Detects Copilot by `api.githubcopilot.com` host, `x-github-token` header, and `editor-version` header. Reports `sessionKind: 'assistant'`.

**`lineagelens-src/agentAdapters/claudeCode.ts`**
Claude Code CLI adapter. Detects Claude Code by `anthropic-version` header combined with `x-app: cli` or `claude-code/` user-agent. Reports `sessionKind: 'cli'` or `'agentic'` depending on whether an agentic session marker is present.

**`lineagelens-src/agentAdapters/codeium.ts`**, **`aider.ts`**, **`continue.ts`**, **`cody.ts`**, **`amazonQ.ts`**, **`geminiCli.ts`**, **`codex.ts`**
Tool-specific adapters. Each detects its tool by a combination of host, headers, and user-agent signals. See the adapter table in Section 2 for the key signals per adapter.

**`lineagelens-src/agentAdapters/legacy.ts`**
Fallback heuristic adapter with order 1000 (always runs last). Uses keyword matching on user-agent and host strings. Returns confidence 0.3 at best (tool name detected by keyword) down to 0.1 (provider only). Never wins over a specific adapter.

**`lineagelens-src/storage/StorageService.ts`**
Abstract interface for provenance record storage. Implementations: `LocalStorageService` (VS Code global state or workspace JSON file, used in Base mode) and `BackendStorageService` (sends records to the FastAPI backend, used in Plus/Max). The extension selects the implementation based on which backend URL is configured.

---

### Universal Proxy (`lineagelens-proxy/`)

**`lineagelens-proxy/proxy.py`**
Transparent HTTP/HTTPS proxy running on port 8788. Intercepts any AI tool that routes its API traffic through it. For HTTP requests, reads the request and response bodies, extracts prompt + response, and POSTs a capture payload to the LineageLens backend at port 8787. For HTTPS CONNECT tunnels, records the routing metadata only (`tunnel_only`). Constructs upstream URLs using `urllib.parse.urlunparse` to prevent URL injection. Designed to be started as a standalone process independent of the VS Code extension. Body size limit is controlled by the `MAX_BODY_BYTES` env var (default 2 MB).

---

### Backend (`lineagelens-backend/`)

**`lineagelens-backend/app/main.py`**
FastAPI application entry point. Registers all routers, configures all middleware (CORS, trusted hosts, security headers, payload size limit, rate limiting), initializes the database engine and session factory, starts the Neo4j service if enabled, and serves the static dashboard HTML. Also exposes the `/health` endpoint and the `/dashboard` file route.

**`lineagelens-backend/app/core/config.py`**
Pydantic `Settings` model loaded from environment variables. Holds all configuration: database URL, JWT secrets, backend mode (`solo`/`team`/`enterprise`), embedding provider, LLM explain settings, Neo4j connection, rate limits, connection pool sizes, CORS origins, and feature flags. Single source of truth for all backend configuration.

**`lineagelens-backend/app/core/security.py`**
JWT authentication. `get_current_auth_context` is the FastAPI dependency used by all protected routes. Validates signature, expiry, audience, issuer, required scopes, and `token_version` (for logout revocation). Returns an `AuthContext` with `workspace_id`, `user_id`, `role`, and `scopes`. `ensure_workspace_scope` enforces that every record operation uses the auth workspace, not the request payload workspace.

**`lineagelens-backend/app/core/mode_guard.py`**
FastAPI dependency `require_non_solo`. Applied to routes that require Plus or higher. Returns HTTP 403 with an upgrade message if `BACKEND_MODE=solo`. Keeps Base mode endpoints disabled without any per-route conditionals.

**`lineagelens-backend/app/core/rate_limit.py`**
In-memory sliding-window rate limiter. Tracks request counts per client IP with a configurable window. Provides `check(key, limit, window_seconds)` → `RateLimitDecision(allowed, remaining, retry_after_seconds)`. Applied by `RequestGuardsMiddleware` for HTTP and `ws_capture.py` for WebSocket connections.

**`lineagelens-backend/app/api/routes/auth.py`**
Authentication routes: `POST /auth/register`, `POST /auth/login`, `POST /auth/refresh`, `GET /auth/me`, `POST /auth/logout`. Handles PBKDF2-SHA256 hashing, password strength validation, username normalization, JWT issuance, refresh token rotation (JTI-based), and token version increment on logout.

**`lineagelens-backend/app/api/routes/ingest.py`**
`POST /ingest` — HTTP fallback ingest route. Accepts a provenance record payload, normalizes it, calls the provenance service, and returns the stored UUID. Used by the VS Code extension when the WebSocket connection is unavailable.

**`lineagelens-backend/app/api/routes/ws_capture.py`**
`WS /ws/capture` — primary ingest channel. Accepts WebSocket connections from the VS Code extension. Each message is a provenance record JSON. Applies per-connection rate limiting (message count + concurrent connection count). Falls back gracefully if the connection drops mid-send.

**`lineagelens-backend/app/api/routes/provenance.py`**
`GET /provenance/{uuid}` — fetch a single record by UUID, workspace-scoped. Returns the full serialized provenance record. Used by the record detail modal in the dashboard and by the `get_record` MCP tool.

**`lineagelens-backend/app/api/routes/search.py`**
`POST /search` — vector or keyword search across workspace records. Accepts `SearchRequest` (query, model, date range, file path, limit, offset). Returns `SearchResponse` (results, count, total, offset, warnings). Plus/Max only; returns 403 in Base mode.

**`lineagelens-backend/app/api/routes/explain.py`**
`POST /explain` — generate a plain-English LLM explanation for a provenance record. Accepts UUID or raw record. Calls `explanation_service.py`. Returns the explanation text, model used, and source. `GET /explain/system-prompt` returns the explanation system prompt for inspection.

**`lineagelens-backend/app/api/routes/insights.py`**
`POST /insights/dashboard` — full governance analytics payload. Calls `get_insights_dashboard_payload`, which fetches up to 2000 records and computes governance summary, compliance controls, hotspots, model analytics, risk trends, agent sessions, and member stats. Results cached 5 minutes per `(workspace_id, search_params)`. Plus/Max only.

**`lineagelens-backend/app/api/routes/report.py`**
`GET /report/usage` — AI usage report endpoint. Reshapes the cached insights payload into a CEO/compliance-friendly summary: total insertions, total AI lines, model usage breakdown, top risky files, developer breakdown, risk distribution, compliance control statuses, and weekly trend. Supports `dateFrom` / `dateTo` query params. Plus/Max only.

**`lineagelens-backend/app/api/routes/team.py`**
`GET /team/members` and `POST /team/invite`. Lists active workspace members with per-user record counts, lines added, and join date. Invite creates a new user in the same workspace (admin-only). Validates password strength and handles concurrent registration races with 409. Plus/Max only.

**`lineagelens-backend/app/api/routes/export.py`**
`GET /export/audit` — admin-only CSV audit export. Filters by `dateFrom`, `dateTo`, `developer`, `filePath`. Streams a CSV file with all matching provenance records. Plus/Max only.

**`lineagelens-backend/app/services/provenance_service.py`**
Core ingest and search service. `store_provenance_record` runs the full ingest pipeline: AST normalization, embedding generation, PostgreSQL write, optional Neo4j write, lineage node ID save-back. `search_provenance_records` handles three search paths: vector (pgvector cosine distance with IVFFLAT), keyword fallback (tokenized scoring), and plain listing — all with offset/limit pagination. `serialize_provenance_record` converts a database row to the API response shape.

**`lineagelens-backend/app/services/ingest_normalizer.py`**
Extracts and normalizes fields from the raw ingest payload. Resolves `workspace_id` from the payload or the authenticated user's workspace. Extracts `inserted_code`, `file_path`, `timestamp`, `prompt_messages`, `model_name`, `raw_model_response`. Warns when no client-provided UUID is present (retry duplication risk). Returns a `NormalizedIngestPayload` dataclass.

**`lineagelens-backend/app/services/embedding_service.py`**
Generates 256-dimensional embedding vectors for provenance records. Two providers: `hash` (deterministic, no API key, suitable for Base mode) and `openai` (calls `text-embedding-3-small`, enables semantic similarity search in Plus/Max). Dimension is configurable via `PGVECTOR_DIMENSION`.

**`lineagelens-backend/app/services/ast_normalizer.py`**
Extracts a structural AST node-type sequence from inserted code. Uses language inference from the file extension. The node-type sequence is language-agnostic (e.g., `["function_declaration", "identifier", "return_statement"]`) and stored in `ast_snapshot` for future similarity matching and lineage detection.

**`lineagelens-backend/app/services/neo4j_service.py`**
Creates and manages Neo4j graph nodes. `ensure_constraints` creates uniqueness constraints on startup. `create_lineage_node` creates `AIGeneratedBlock` and `ProvenanceBlockVersion` nodes and the `HAS_VERSION` / `LATEST_VERSION` relationships. `delete_lineage_node` is called on Postgres commit failure to clean up orphaned nodes. Only active when `NEO4J_ENABLED=true`.

**`lineagelens-backend/app/services/explanation_service.py`**
Generates plain-English explanations of provenance records. Builds a structured system prompt describing the inserted code, prompt context, agent session, and risk score. Calls an OpenAI-compatible `/chat/completions` endpoint. Falls back to a deterministic template when `EXPLAIN_LLM_API_KEY` is not set. Template fallback extracts key facts (file, model, risk, lines) without any API call.

**`lineagelens-backend/app/services/insights_service.py`**
Computes the full governance analytics payload. `get_insights_dashboard_payload` fetches up to 2000 records and applies a 5-minute TTL in-memory cache keyed by `(workspace_id, search_params_hash)`. `build_insights_dashboard` does the CPU-intensive work: risk scoring every record, computing compliance controls, building hotspots, model analytics, risk trends, and agent session grouping. Risk scoring evaluates 9 pattern categories (secrets, commands, eval, SQL, auth, filesystem, network, exception handling, path signals).

**`lineagelens-backend/app/services/team_service.py`**
Builds `TeamMemberStats` objects from `UserAccount` rows and per-user record counts and net lines added. Returns data used by `GET /team/members` and included in the insights dashboard `memberStats` field.

**`lineagelens-backend/app/services/websocket_manager.py`**
Manages the set of active WebSocket connections for `/ws/capture`. Tracks connection count per workspace and enforces the `RATE_LIMIT_WS_MAX_CONNECTIONS` limit. Provides `connect`, `disconnect`, and `broadcast` methods.

**`lineagelens-backend/app/db/models.py`**
SQLAlchemy ORM models for the two database tables: `ProvenanceRecord` (one row per AI insertion, with `embedding_vector` pgvector column) and `UserAccount` (one row per user, with `token_version` for logout revocation). Defines all column types, indexes, and constraints.

**`lineagelens-backend/app/db/session.py`**
SQLAlchemy async engine and session factory. `create_engine_from_settings` builds the asyncpg engine with the configured pool settings. `get_db_session` is the FastAPI dependency that provides a scoped async session per request. `initialize_database` runs Alembic migrations on startup.

**`lineagelens-backend/app/schemas/provenance.py`**
Pydantic schemas for all provenance API request and response shapes: `IngestRequest`, `SearchRequest` (with `offset` for pagination), `SearchResponse` (with `total`, `offset`), `SearchResultItem`, `ProvenanceResponse`, `IngestResponse`, `ExplainRequest`, `ExplainResponse`.

**`lineagelens-backend/alembic/versions/`**
Alembic migration files run in order at startup:
- `202501150001` — initial schema: `provenance_records` + `user_accounts` + pgvector extension + base indexes
- `202501160001` — adds `role` to users, `user_id` FK to records
- `202501170001` — backfills `role='member'` for existing users
- `202501180001` — seeds first user per workspace as admin
- `202501190001` — adds `token_version` to users
- `202501200001` — adds `refresh_token_jti` to users
- `202501210001` — adds IVFFLAT index on `embedding_vector` for fast ANN vector search

**`lineagelens-backend/app/static/dashboard.html`**
Full single-page dashboard application served at `/dashboard`. No build step — vanilla HTML/CSS/JS + Chart.js 4 via CDN. Eight tabs: Governance Overview, Timeline (Chart.js bar+line), Graph (force-directed canvas), Live Feed (30s poll with badge), Search, Record Viewer, Export, Team. Record Detail Modal, theme toggle (dark/light), backend status dot, MCP status indicator.

