### CLI (`lineagelens-cli/`)

**`lineagelens-cli/src/commands/lineagelens-cli-start.js`**
`lineagelens start --mode <base|plus|max>` — runs the correct `docker compose up --detach` command for the specified tier. Checks Docker is running, validates the compose file exists, and prints the dashboard URL on success.

**`lineagelens-cli/src/commands/lineagelens-cli-stop.js`**
`lineagelens stop --mode <base|plus|max>` — stops the specified tier's containers. Optionally removes volumes with `--volumes`.

**`lineagelens-cli/src/commands/lineagelens-cli-status.js`**
`lineagelens status` — shows container health for all three tiers. Runs `docker compose ps` for each and prints a summary table.

**`lineagelens-cli/src/commands/lineagelens-cli-logs.js`**
`lineagelens logs --mode <tier> [--service <name>]` — tails logs for a tier or a specific service container. Runs `docker compose logs --follow`.

**`lineagelens-cli/src/utils/lineagelens-cli-docker.js`**
Docker availability check and `docker compose` command runner. Wraps `node:child_process` `spawn` calls.

**`lineagelens-cli/src/utils/lineagelens-cli-env.js`**
Environment helpers: resolves the `.env` file path for a given tier, reads config values, and validates required variables are present.

