### Scripts (`lineagelens-scripts/`)

**`lineagelens-scripts/quickstart-{base,plus,max}.sh`**
7-step automated first-time setup for each tier. Checks prerequisites (docker, openssl, curl, python3), stops existing containers, generates or validates `.env` secrets, starts PostgreSQL, waits for health, runs Alembic migrations, starts the backend, waits for `/health` 200, prints the health response and getting-started commands.

**`lineagelens-scripts/reset-{base,plus,max}.sh`**
Destroys all containers, volumes, and data for a tier. Removes `.env`. Use only for a full reset.

**`lineagelens-scripts/debug.sh`**
Automated health check script. Runs PASS/FAIL checks for: Docker availability, compose config validity, database migration status, backend startup, and HTTP health endpoint. Prints a summary with colour-coded results.

**`lineagelens-scripts/commands-plus.md`**
Complete command reference for the Plus tier: CLI commands, Docker Compose commands, dashboard login, authentication API, proxy setup, team management API, provenance API, health diagnostics, MCP server setup, troubleshooting guide.

**`lineagelens-scripts/commands-max.md`**
Complete command reference for the Max tier: all Plus commands plus Neo4j-specific commands (Cypher shell, Browser, memory config), Neo4j troubleshooting, MCP server setup with Max-specific notes (`get_record` returns `lineageNodeId`).

**`lineagelens-scripts/package-{base,plus,max}.ps1`**
PowerShell packaging scripts for Windows. Bundle the VSIX, compose file, scripts, and documentation into a release zip for each tier.

**`lineagelens-scripts/release.ps1`**
Master release script. Runs `vsce package` to build the VSIX, then calls each packaging script to produce the three release bundles.

**`lineagelens-scripts/run-backend-native.ps1`**
Runs the FastAPI backend natively (without Docker) on Windows. Sets up the Python virtual environment, installs dependencies, runs Alembic migrations, and starts uvicorn.

**`lineagelens-scripts/test-backend-native.ps1`**
Health-checks a natively running backend. Calls `/health` and prints the response.

**`lineagelens-scripts/use-lineagelens-proxy.ps1`**
Sets `ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL` and `OPENAI_BASE_URL` environment variables in the current PowerShell session to route AI tool traffic through the universal proxy at port 8788.
